<article class="env-definition" id="030L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/030L">Definition <span data-tag="030L">9.14.7</span>.</a> Let $E/F$ be an algebraic field extension. Let $E_{sep}$ be the subextension found in Lemma <a href="/tag/030K" data-tag="030K">9.14.6</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The integer $[E_{sep} : F]$ is called the <em>separable degree</em> of the extension. Notation $[E : F]_ s$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The integer $[E : E_{sep}]$ is called the <em>inseparable degree</em>, or the <em>degree of inseparability</em> of the extension. Notation $[E : F]_ i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>